Overlay patch 0046 (visionOS Phase 02): stereo comfort exports — the SM64
analog of the Ship of Harkinian port 0032, radically smaller. SM64 keeps the camera in
the MODELVIEW stack (perspective-only G_MTX_PROJECTION), so 0045 derives
the whole stereo fold from the projection matrix itself: no camera basis,
no P00 export. The game only writes, once per rendered frame in
geo_process_perspective (runs on every screen incl. menus — a
level_update-side hook would go stale on the title screen):
- gSoh3DCamDist: gLakituState.focusDistance (refreshed every update at
  camera.c:3108) — drives 0045's adaptive convergence;
- gSoh3DPaused: pause/course-complete menu up (sCurrPlayMode !=
  PLAY_MODE_NORMAL || gMenuMode != MENU_MODE_NONE);
- gSoh3DInPlay: the port's own "actively in play" precedent (the mirror-
  mode gate in this same function): PLAY_MODE_NORMAL && Mario exists with
  a nonzero action && not credits — 0045 flattens stereo on title/file
  select through this (the goddard head folds lookat INTO projection);
- gSoh3DAiming: first-person C-up camera (gCamera->mode ==
  CAMERA_MODE_C_UP) — 0045's aiming comfort profile.
Globals are defined by the shell (SohIosShell.m); __IOS__-gated, desktop
oracle unchanged. camera.h include added for gLakituState/gCamera/mode.

